# /// script
# requires-python = ">=3.11"
# dependencies = ["pyyaml>=6"]
# ///
"""Live dashboard for mausi — meant to sit in kitty tab 1.

Sessions: one row per kitty tab running Claude — tab number, ⏳ when it is
waiting on you, ▶ (green) while Claude is working (hooks: prompt → Stop), › the
tab you are on; then
Jira ticket (+ summary when JIRA_API_USER/TOKEN are set), git
branch, cwd, short session id, and how long since the transcript last moved.

You (top of Now): time since my last break — a pause of 5+ minutes between
messages I type to Claude in any session counts as one — yellow from 50 min, red
from 60; today's active time (gaps up to 15 min) and a late
warning after 20:00; this week's gave/took count and the latest entries from
the energy log ([energy] log). L logs a new entry (activity, state, valence).

Infra: running docker containers; k3d clusters when there are any; and the
current kubectl context — node status, one row per pod (kube-system folded
away while healthy) with ready/status/age/restarts and its ingress host.

Notifications (top of Work, Linux): the last few hours of desktop notifications
from the log mausi-notif-capture writes, minus Claude's own alerts, with
repeats collapsed; Enter opens the app they came from.

Work (optional, config [board]): my open PRs, merged PRs still to close in
Jira, open Jira issues — read from a local board's /api/dash.json, which
caches gh/Jira and holds the Jira token, so nothing is fetched twice.

Today and Mail (optional, config [commands]): the output of the calendar and
mail commands, as JSON. Sections without a configured source are left out.

Two views: "Now" (Today, Sessions, tasks, Infra) and "Work" (PRs, Jira),
side by side when the window is at least TWO_COLUMN_WIDTH wide (Tab or ←/→
moves the cursor between the columns), one at a time (Tab switches) when not. j/k or ↑/↓ move the cursor over actionable rows and Enter
acts on the selected row — opens the PR / Jira ticket / container port / pod
ingress / meeting's Meet in the browser, jumps to a session's tab, or opens a
task on the web board. z (or Enter on a section's heading) zooms that section to
full screen with more detail — every pod and container, 24h of notifications
with their text, all of tasks.md, tomorrow's meetings; z/Esc/q goes back.
In a zoomed section / filters it as you type (every word must match; Enter keeps
the filter, Enter on an empty one or Esc afterwards clears it).
The mouse wheel moves the cursor in the column under the pointer (or scrolls
an open pop-up); hold Shift to select text with the mouse.
Notes (Work): snippets from ~/notes/snippets.md ("## title" + the text) and
quick notes from ~/notes/notes.md. Enter copies one to the clipboard,
a saves the clipboard as a new snippet (you type the title), n takes a quick
note, e opens the file at that entry in $EDITOR (vim) as a kitty overlay (on a
task, tasks.md at that task), d deletes one (after a y/N confirm).
c on a task, Jira ticket, PR or notification opens a new kitty tab with a
Claude session primed with that row's details (in the ticket's worktree if any).
d hides one notification, D all up to now (kept in ~/.cache/mausi/
dismissed.json; the capture log is untouched, and zoom still lists them dimmed).
Tasks: d on a task moves it from Open to Done in ~/.claude/tasks.md (after a
y/N confirm), u undoes the last one. p pins a task to the top of a "### Now"
section (shown first here); p on a pinned task sends it back where it came from.
+/- move a task up/down within its section.
Space shows the row's full text in a pop-up — for the
notification bodies and titles that are cut off. s on a Docker container or pod opens a shell in it
(docker/kubectl exec, bash if present else sh) in a new kitty tab. w on a
Jira ticket, PR or task naming one opens its worktree (<worktrees>/<repo>-<KEY>,
created by the configured worktree command if needed) with Claude, in a new tab. A view taller than the window scrolls with the cursor.

Keys: Tab switch view · j/k ↑/↓ move · Enter open · 1-9 / 0 jump to that tab ·
g tab picker · m join the current/next meeting · o open the web board ·
r refresh now · q quit.
Infra is refreshed in a background thread because kubectl against a dead
cluster can take seconds; the session list redraws every couple of seconds.
"""
